==Trivia==
*Vermilingua means "worm tongue" and is the taxonomic suborder of animals commonly known as anteaters.
*The "Rang" in Rangmaster's name comes from Rangurotora (ラングロトラ), the Japanese name of ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Volvidon|Volvidon]], which shares Rangmaster's ears, eye color, carapace and long, powerful tongue. When Rangmaster attacks, his tongue is shown to crackle with electricity, which may be a reference to the Paralysis effect that Volvidon can inflict (in ''Monster Hunter'' and many other games, paralysis is represented by electricity).
**Although it was localized as "Rang" in this enemy's English name, ラング ''rangu'' can also be taken as ''langue'' (French for tongue; "Languemaster" would mean "Tonguemaster").
*Aside from Volvidon, Rangmaster's design may have been inspired by [[wikipedia:Pangolin|pangolins]], long-tongued armored mammals also known as scaly anteaters.

